# Project One Get-Item Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: get-item and inventory design for M7 Project Two
#
# Review the course-provided get-item flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, SET, ADD, or similar terms.

START get_item
Prompt player:
"Enter item name to collect item"

Input itemChoice

IF current room contains itemChoice THEN

    Add itemChoice to inventory

    Remove item from room

    Display:
    "Item added to inventory"

ELSE

    Display:
    "That item is not in this room."

END IF
   
END get_item


# References

Main Game Flow 
START GAME

Set current room to Command Center

Create empty inventory

WHILE player has not won or lost

    Display current room
    Display inventory

    IF current room contains item THEN
        Display room item
    END IF

    Ask player for command
    (Move or Get Item)

    Process command

    IF player enters villain room THEN

        IF inventory contains all 6 items THEN
            Display "You defeated NEXUS! You win!"
            End game

        ELSE
            Display "NEXUS captured you! Game Over!"
            End game

        END IF

    END IF

END WHILE

END GAME

